{title: Copper Kettle Blues}
{artist: Hollis Grey}
{key: Em}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Em]Mama’s copper kettl[C]e on the stove
[G]‘Round the kitchen ev[D]erybody knows
[Em]“Don’t you let it boil [C]dry,” she’d say
[G]Then she’d hum th[D]e morning bl[Em]ues away
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Copper kettle blu[G]es
[D]Whistling out the ne[Em]ws
[C]Nothing left to lo[G]se
[D]Copper kettle blues[Em]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Em]Now the kettle’s sitt[C]ing on my shelf
[G]Dented like the rest o[D]f us, itself
[Em]“Polish it on Sundays,[C]” that’s her rule
[G]Every scratch a less[D]on from a sch[Em]ool
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Copper kettle blu[G]es
[D]Whistling out the ne[Em]ws
[C]Nothing left to lo[G]se
[D]Copper kettle blues[Em]
{end_of_chorus}
